<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">01 · Reach-in cooler not cooling</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three root causes our techs diagnose first across LA commercial.</h2>

    <p>A commercial reach-in cooler that won't hold below 41°F usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA County restaurant cook lines, hotel back-of-house breakfast prep, hospital food service lines, school cafeteria back-of-house, and ghost kitchen operations. (1) Condenser fan motor failure year 5 to 9 — the most common single reach-in service item across all brands. Head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops, cabinet temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock. (2) Dirty condenser coil — restaurant kitchen grease and lint accumulate on the rear-mount or top-mount condenser fins. About 25 to 30 percent of reach-in service calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Evaporator fan motor failure year 5 to 9 — no airflow across the coil, cold air doesn't circulate, product near the coil stays cold while product near the door warms. $320 to $520 replacement.</p>

    <p>This page covers commercial reach-in cooler not-cooling diagnostic across all major brands — True Manufacturing (T-23, T-49, T-72 — Trulaske family commercial), Beverage-Air (HR1, HR2, HR3 — Ali Group), Traulsen (G-Series, R-Series, RH, RIH — ITW Food Equipment Group), Hoshizaki (CR-Series standard, HR-Series premium inverter), Continental Refrigerator (D2, D3, D4), Delfield (Welbilt), Turbo-Air (M3R, M3F, MSR), Perlick (HP15, HP24 back-bar), Victory, Migali, Norlake, Avantco, Maxx Cold. Reach-in repair tier substantially lower than walk-in scale because of smaller equipment scale — most reach-in repairs fall in the $400 to $1,500 range vs $800 to $3,200 walk-in scale. See sister page <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a> for walk-in scale diagnostic.</p>

    <p><strong>$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair.</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573 and EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), plus R-290 propane certification. CSLB C-20 HVAC. BBB Accredited Business. 90-day warranty. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Next-day Riverside and San Bernardino. Sister sub-services: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/commercial-freezer-not-freezing/">commercial freezer not freezing</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/reach-in-cooler-repair/">reach-in cooler repair pillar</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/not-cooling/">generic commercial refrigeration not cooling</a>. Parent: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/">commercial refrigeration</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 DIAGNOSTIC SEQUENCE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Five-step diagnostic on every reach-in cooler not-cooling call</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Cheap-first sequence across all major brands.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Box temperature documentation.</strong> Probe at product level (not air space at ceiling) to verify current product temperature against operator log entry. Establishes HACCP CCP exceedance window for California Retail Food Code 41°F compliance.</li>
      <li><strong>Identify brand and refrigerant.</strong> True / Beverage-Air / Traulsen / Hoshizaki / Continental / Delfield / Turbo-Air / Perlick / Victory / Migali / Norlake. Rating label refrigerant (R-134a legacy or R-290 propane post-2018) determines sealed-system service certification requirement.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual condenser inspection.</strong> Rear-mount or top-mount condenser. Grease, dust, lint accumulation on fins. If condenser is the diagnosis, cleaning runs $200 to $280 and resolves the call without parts on 25 to 30 percent of LA reach-in service visits.</li>
      <li><strong>Condenser fan motor amp draw and rotation.</strong> Multimeter at fan motor terminals against rated spec, visual rotation check. Most common single reach-in service item across all brands. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock for common shaded-pole motor sizes.</li>
      <li><strong>Evaporator fan motor airflow check plus door gasket verification.</strong> Evap fan failure year 5 to 9 equals zoned warm/cold within same cabinet. Door gasket year 5 to 7 allows warm humid LA kitchen air infiltration.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Most diagnostics complete in 25 to 40 minutes on-site. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk operators through the findings with photo documentation before any repair work begins. Sealed-system work on R-290 propane reach-in models requires both EPA 608 Universal certification (#1346255700410) and R-290 hydrocarbon certification.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TOP CAUSES FREQUENCY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Top causes by frequency</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Across LA County reach-in cooler service calls.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County commercial reach-in cooler service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run — Sunset Strip restaurant cook lines with True T-49 reach-ins, DTLA hotel back-of-house breakfast prep with Beverage-Air HR2, Beverly Hills luxury hospitality with Traulsen G-Series, sushi bars across Sawtelle and Little Tokyo with Hoshizaki CR-Series, hospital food service lines with Traulsen RIH hospital-grade, school cafeteria back-of-house with Continental D3, ghost kitchens and food trucks with compact Turbo-Air M3R — the failure breakdown clusters predictably across all brands.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Condenser fan motor failure (25-30% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Most common single reach-in service item across all brands. Year 5 to 9 typical wear curve. Head pressure climbs without fan circulation, cooling capacity drops, cabinet temperature drifts up. $320 to $520 replacement, same-day from truck stock.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Dirty condenser coil (20-25% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulate on condenser fins. Resolves at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning on 25 to 30 percent of reach-in service calls, no parts charge. Standalone deep cleaning $200 to $280.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Evaporator fan motor failure (15-20% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Year 5 to 9 typical wear curve. No airflow across the evaporator coil, cold air doesn't circulate, product near the coil stays cold while product near the door warms. Customer reports zones of warm and cold within same cabinet. $320 to $520 replacement.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Door gasket year 5-7 (12-15% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Compression set, tearing, magnetic seal failure. Warm air infiltration, defrost cycle overwhelmed. $180 to $340 replacement covering True T-23/T-49/T-72, Beverage-Air HR1/HR2/HR3, Traulsen G/R, Hoshizaki CR/HR, Continental D2/D3/D4, Delfield, Turbo-Air M3R dimensions stocked on truck.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Refrigerant leak (8-12% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Suction line or evaporator inlet pinhole, joint failure, vibration fatigue at copper fittings. Symptom: gradual loss of cooling capacity over weeks. Requires EPA 608 Universal certified work — leak detection (electronic sniffer, UV dye where applicable), evacuation to deep vacuum, recharge with correct refrigerant (R-134a legacy or R-290 propane post-2018). $700 to $1,500 typical all-in.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>6. Compressor failure year 8-12 (5-8% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Compressor runs continuously without bringing cabinet down, or short-cycles, or audible knocking. $1,400 to $2,400 all-in including EPA 608 refrigerant recovery, system evacuation, new compressor, fresh refrigerant charge, pressure test. On year 12+ units our techs walk through repair-vs-replace math with the operator.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

